- One flip takes 90ms. In its first half the top flap (the old character's top half) falls forward: rotateX from 0 to −90deg with ease-in-quad, hinged at its bottom edge; behind it the static top already shows the new character's top. In its second half the bottom flap (the new character's bottom half) lands: rotateX from 90deg to 0 with ease-out-quad, hinged at its top edge, covering the old bottom. A moving flap is darkened: filter brightness(1 − 0.45 × how far it is from flat, 0 to 1). The tiles use perspective 5 × the tile height and backface-visibility: hidden.
- To show a message, tile i (left to right) starts flipping 30ms × i later, then flips one character after another, back to back, until it reaches its character.
- When every tile has landed, the message stays 5s, then the board flips to the next message (looping). A click or tap skips to the next message right away.
- Tile width = min(3.6rem, 90% of the section width ÷ (tiles + (tiles − 1) × 0.08)); tile height = 1.5 × the width; tiles sit in one row, 0.08 × the tile width apart, centered in a full-screen section (100svh, at least 540px).
- A tile is a rounded rectangle (radius 0.1 × its width) in the surface color; its character is Anybody weight 700, font size 0.54 × the tile height, centered, in the main text color, with line-height equal to the tile height. Each half is an element with overflow: hidden showing the top or bottom half of the character, and a 0.025 × tile height line in the background color separates the halves.
- Run one requestAnimationFrame loop. dt = seconds since the last frame, clamped to 0.05; t = seconds the loop has run (the sum of dt). Flip times use t; a tile that falls behind does several flips in one frame.
- The first message starts flipping in when the animation starts. Recompute tile sizes on every resize.
- Reduced-motion still frame: the first message, every flap at rest.

## How people interact
- A click or tap (on release) anywhere on the section skips to the next message.

## Where this goes
Create a single index.html file with all CSS and JavaScript inline, ready to open by double-clicking it. Don't use any libraries or build tools.

## Rules
- Smooth on a mid-range laptop and a phone: one requestAnimationFrame loop, batched canvas drawing, devicePixelRatio capped at 2, pause when off-screen.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion: start paused and show a meaningful still frame, with a visible Play/Pause button.
- Accessible: real buttons, visible keyboard focus, text contrast of at least 4.5:1, decorative canvases hidden from screen readers.
- Works on touch screens without blocking vertical scrolling.

## When you're done
Keep the explanation short: list the files and the key parameters I can tweak."
`;

